---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import Panel from '../components/Panel.astro';
---
<Site title="Privacy policy | DNA4Digital" description="How dna4digital.com handles your personal data.">
  <Panel rung={4} kicker="Privacy policy">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">Last updated: October 2026. Nothing that tracks you runs on this site until you agree to it in the cookie banner, and you can change your choice at any time.</p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>The controller of your personal data is Daniel Nowak, trading as DNA4Digital. For anything about your data, email <a href="mailto:dn@dna4digital.com">dn@dna4digital.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>What I collect and why</h2>
    <p><strong>Contact form.</strong> When you send a message I receive your name, email address, optional company name, the topic you picked, your message and, if you came from the AI readiness test, your score. I use this only to reply to you and, if we decide to work together, to prepare and run that work. The legal basis is your consent and steps taken at your request before entering into a contract (GDPR Article 6(1)(a) and (b)).</p>
    <p><strong>AI readiness test.</strong> The test runs entirely in your browser and doesn't store or send your answers. I only see your score if you choose to send it through the contact form.</p>
    <p><strong>Analytics, only with your consent.</strong> If you allow analytics, Google Analytics records which pages you visit, how you got here, roughly where you are (country and city), and the type of device and browser you use. I use this to see which pages are useful. It does not tell me who you are. The legal basis is your consent (Article 6(1)(a)).</p>
    <p><strong>Visit history and enquiries, only with your consent.</strong> If you allow marketing, HubSpot records the pages you visit. If you then contact me, those visits are linked to your enquiry in my CRM so I can reply with the right context, and HubSpot may also record the details you enter in the contact form. The legal basis is your consent (Article 6(1)(a)).</p>
    <p><strong>Technical data.</strong> Like any website, the servers that deliver this site process your IP address and basic request details (browser type, time, page requested) to deliver pages, protect the site from abuse and limit form spam. The legal basis is my legitimate interest in running a secure website (Article 6(1)(f)). I don't use this data to profile you.</p>

    <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
    <p><strong>Always on, stored only in your browser:</strong> your language choice, your cookie choice and your accessibility settings. They are kept in local storage, are never sent to me and are needed for the site to work the way you asked.</p>
    <p><strong>Only with your consent:</strong></p>
    <ul class="ticks">
      <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> (analytics): cookies <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>, which distinguish visits and last up to two years.</li>
      <li><strong>HubSpot</strong> (marketing): cookies <code>__hstc</code>, <code>hubspotutk</code>, <code>__hssc</code> and <code>__hssrc</code>, which recognise returning visits and last up to six months.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Until you choose, everything except the always-on items is switched off and Google Tag Manager, which loads these tools, is not loaded at all. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time with <button type="button" class="linkbtn" data-open-settings="privacy">Cookie &amp; accessibility settings</button>, also linked at the bottom of every page. Withdrawing removes these cookies from your browser.</p>
    <p>Fonts and scripts for the site itself are served from this domain, not from third-party CDNs.</p>

    <h2>Who processes the data for me</h2>
    <ul class="ticks">
      <li><strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> hosts the site and delivers contact form messages by email.</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> (Google Workspace) hosts my mailbox, where your messages arrive.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Ireland Limited</strong> provides Google Analytics and Google Tag Manager, only if you consent.</li>
      <li><strong>HubSpot Ireland Limited</strong> and <strong>HubSpot, Inc.</strong> provide my CRM and visit tracking, only if you consent. HubSpot data is hosted in the EU.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Cloudflare, Google and HubSpot may process data outside the European Economic Area. Where they do, the transfer is covered by the EU-US Data Privacy Framework or the European Commission's standard contractual clauses.</p>

    <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
    <p>Messages are kept for as long as needed to handle your enquiry and any work that follows from it, and to meet legal obligations such as accounting rules. After that they are deleted. Analytics data is kept for the retention period set in Google Analytics and then deleted automatically. HubSpot records are kept while we are in touch or work together, and deleted when they are no longer needed.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under the GDPR you can ask to access, correct or delete your data, restrict or object to its processing, receive it in a portable format, and withdraw consent at any time without affecting what was done before. Email <a href="mailto:dn@dna4digital.com">dn@dna4digital.com</a> and I'll respond within one month.</p>
    <p>If you think your data has been handled unlawfully, you can complain to a data protection authority, for example the President of the Personal Data Protection Office (UODO) in Poland or the authority in your country of residence.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If I change this policy, I'll publish the new version on this page with an updated date.</p>
  </Panel>
</Site>
